I wrote a chunk of code that allows shopkeepers to perform extra services
for the player like identifying, uncursing, enchanting weapons, etc.
I think it's a lot of fun (adds to the game) and it gives the player a
REASON TO COLLECT GOLD!  The way it works is if you hit (p) to pay the
shopkeeper, and if you don't owe him any money, then he'll present you a
list of other services he provides:

Service		Comments/Restrictions
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
identify	Identify items in your pack.  All shopkeepers can do this.
		However, if a shopkeeper specializes in a certain type of
		item and tries to identify a different class of item, he
		may fail.  E.g. a wand shop tries to identify a ring.

appraise	Appraise weapon's worth.  Which is better, a trident or
		a battle axe?  The shopkeeper can tell you.  General
		store and weapon shops only.

uncurse		Uncurse an item in your pack.  All shops.

weapon-works	Rustproof/enchant weapon for a price.  Weapon shops only.
		If item is "poisonable" then that's an option as well.

armor-works	Rustproof/enchant armor.

charge		Wand shops, ring shops, and tool shops.
		Expensive, but better than scroll of charging.

